Fork PR (same branch, for browsing): https://github.com/AlexPerrin/OpenRune-Server/pull/18

## Summary

There were no random events. This adds the Genie random event in a new module `content/events/random-events`, scheduled by the OSRS Wiki's random event spawn mechanics ("Random events", section "Spawn mechanics", which quotes Mod Ash for each rule). Content area from #353. This push replaces the first version with a rewrite checked against the wiki, on current `main` (`829b9477d`).

- **When.** The next event is due 1-2 hours after the last one, on a real-time clock that keeps running while the player is logged out. The due time is stored in a persistent player attribute (`random_event_next_at`, epoch milliseconds), so it survives logout and restarts. A soft timer checks every 5 minutes of play (500 ticks) whether it is due.
- **Offline.** If the event came due while the player was offline, the due time moves forward by 10-70 minutes on login, as many times as needed to land in the future, and keeps counting.
- **Where not.** When it is due and the player is somewhere random events are not allowed, the event is missed and a new 1-2 hours is rolled. The places covered: inside a bank with a bank booth (a booth within 7 tiles) or in front of a bank chest (within 2 tiles), except Ferox Enclave; the Grand Exchange's stone square; the God Wars Dungeon, Ancient Cavern, Waterbirth Island Dungeon, Ruins of Tapoyauik and Charred Dungeon (cache areas); and instances (boss lairs and minigames run in instances here).
- **Transformed.** No event while the player's model is altered (transformation ring, greegree): it is missed in the same way. A Genie that is already out leaves at once if the player transforms (Mod Ash: "the genie would delete itself when it realised you'd equipped that").
- **Busy.** An open interface or a Make-X repeat (a pending weak queue, which is how Make-X loops run here) holds a due event back. It is retried every tick and spawns as soon as the player is free.
- **One at a time.** No second event NPC while the Genie is out.
- **The Genie**: appears beside the player, faces them and says "Greetings, Master/Mistress <name>!". Every 12 seconds he follows them, banks included (wiki, 1 November 2023), and calls them by name with one of the three transcript lines. Talk-to gives the lamp with the transcript's line; the lamp is given as the dialogue opens, and the Genie leaves when it closes or 12 seconds (20 ticks) after Talk-to, whichever is first, so an interrupted Talk-to never loses the lamp or leaves him behind. Talked to again before he goes, he says "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress." (Transcript:Genie, completed event). Dismiss sends him away. He leaves after a minute with "Maybe later." when ignored. Another player's Talk-to gets "Sorry, I'm trying to talk to someone else, but he/she seems to be ignoring me." (the owner's pronoun).
- **The lamp:** Rub gives 10 x the chosen skill's level in XP, multiplied by the world's XP rate like other XP (`statAdvance`, as upstream's quest lamp does). With a full inventory it is dropped at the player's feet for 3 hours (wiki trivia, Mod Ash: rewards are dropped and stay up to three hours).
- `::randomevent` summons him (like `::star`), bypassing the schedule.

New server-only gamevals: timers `random_event` (the 5-minute check) and `random_event_genie` (the Genie's calls), written as `-1` and assigned by `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py` (65534 and 65533, one below the cannon PR's timer so the two don't clash).

