## How it was tested

Unit/integration: `GenieRandomEventTest` (8, integration), on the schedule and the lamp hand-over (AGENTS.md):
- the due time is 1-2 h ahead, persisted, and a relog does not restart it;
- an event due while offline moves 10-70 min forward;
- a due event spawns him and rolls the next one;
- in a bank (booth 2 tiles away) it is missed and re-rolled;
- transformed: missed, and a Genie already out leaves;
- an open interface delays it until closed;
- a Make-X weak queue delays it;
- an interrupted hand-over still gives exactly one lamp, and the Genie leaves.

On this branch: the random-events module's `spotlessCheck`, `test` and `integration` pass (`GenieRandomEventTest` 8/8) after `freshCache` and `buildCache`; `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts. Full build, all tests (764 + 87 integration) and boot to "Server ready" pass on this commit in our QA run.

In game (desktop RuneLite on a branch server, fresh account, on the previous commit; the code differs only in the repeat-Talk-to line and the late-completion guard):
- `::randomevent`: the Genie appears beside the player, follows within 12 s when they walk away, and is gone a minute later when ignored.
- Talk-to: the lamp arrives as the line opens; the Genie is gone within 12 s, also when the dialogue is left open or another one replaces it; exactly one lamp each time.
- A second Talk-to before he goes gave nothing on that commit; on this one it gives "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress.".
- `::randomevent` with a Genie out: "Your Genie is already here."; Dismiss removes him.
- Full inventory: exactly one lamp on the floor under the player.
- Rub: 10 x the skill level x the world's XP rate.
- Scheduling: too slow to wait for in game (1-2 h); the tests cover it.

## Checklist

- [x] Builds and the server boots
- [x] Tests only cover complex logic and anything that moves items (no dupes)
- [ ] Gamevals symbols instead of raw ids; game data in the cache, not Kotlin maps: gamevals symbols throughout, but `RandomEventLocations` keeps its location rules in Kotlin (the no-event dungeon areas, Ferox Enclave as a bank with events, the Grand Exchange square and the bank radii). Areas themselves are cache data (`.data/raw-cache/map/area`), but I found no upstream pattern for a list of area ids or a radius in the cache (no dbtable/pack config for area lists). Happy to move them if you point me at the place you want them.
- [ ] State in varbits/varps, not attrs: the due time is a persistent attribute (epoch milliseconds don't fit a 32-bit varp); happy to switch to a varp holding epoch minutes
- [ ] Matches the OSRS wiki (deviations noted in `docs/quirks.md`): the deviations are listed below, not in `docs/quirks.md`
- [ ] New content checked against rsprox dumps where possible (anims, projectiles, sounds, timings): we have no dumps of the official game
- [x] No unrelated or hand-edited generated changes

## Screenshots / notes for reviewers

Data sources: OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): "Random events" (Spawn mechanics, Locations without random events, Bank locations with random events, Changes, Trivia), "Genie" (incl. Changes), "Transcript:Genie", "Lamp". The spawn rules on the wiki cite Mod Ash's posts, archived on the wiki. As a reference only (2004 RuneScape, not OSRS), LostCity's content scripts (MIT, https://github.com/LostCityRS/Content) for the order of the lamp and the departure on Talk-to.

Deviations, guesses and gaps:
- Approximated: the official no-event zones are hand-drawn and not published. Banks are found from bank booths and chests nearby (radii 7 and 2 are ours), the Grand Exchange square is a 27 x 27 box around the wiki's map centre, and instances stand in for "most bosses and minigames". Not covered: the wiki's other entries (Forestry events, Camdozaal golem workshop, Lake Molch, Shayzien Agility Course, Death's Office, Goblin Cave, Stranglewood, The Scar, POH building mode, boats, PvP worlds, Wintertodt prison, the listed minigames that are not instances here; from "most bosses and combat areas": Abyssal Nexus, Crash Site Cavern, Neypotzli, and Ape Atoll while in greegree form), the per-event restrictions (underwater, Kalphite Lair, Hunter areas). None of these matter for the Genie alone except as places where he can still appear. Of the wiki's "Bank locations with random events", only Ferox Enclave is excepted; the others (Giants' Foundry, the Hosidius charcoal furnaces, Myths' Guild, Rogues' Den, Trouble Brewing, the Sunbleak Island, Wyrmscraig and Charred Island bank chests, Odovacar in Tarn's Lair) count as no-event banks here.
- Guesses: missing the event while transformed (the wiki only says it "will not spawn"), and re-rolling 1-2 h when an event comes due while the Genie is still out. Treating any pending weak queue as a Make-X repeat. The 1-tick retry while busy (the wiki: it turns up "soon after" the menu closes). The 5-minute check counts from login.
- Leaving after a minute is the wiki's (Random events: an ignored event "disappears after a minute"). Guess: the call every 12 seconds; the wiki gives 12 s only for the event before the Optional Randoms update.
- Every random event is a Genie here. In OSRS each event is picked with equal weight from all the events the player is eligible for (Spawn mechanics), so the Genie itself comes far less often than every 1-2 hours. Other events can be added on the same schedule.
- The due time is a persistent attribute, not a varp: epoch milliseconds don't fit a 32-bit varp. Happy to switch to a varp holding epoch minutes if you prefer.
- Guess: the lamp arrives as the Genie's line opens and his departure does not wait on the dialogue. Not on the wiki; LostCity's 2004 content scripts (`macro events/scripts/general/macro_event_genie.rs2`) do the same, adding the lamp before the line and queueing the departure separately.
- Unsourced: the lamp uses the base (unboosted) level. The wiki says "level" (Lamp) and "current level" (Genie), and neither says whether boosts count. "Your wish has been granted!" on Rub, and no chat message when the lamp is given (since 9 September 2021 the game says what you received, but the wording is not on the wiki). "He isn't interested in you." on another player's Dismiss.
- Not implemented: the transcript's "Have a nice day, Master/Mistress." when talked to in a zone without random events (the Genie still gives the lamp there; the completed-event case is implemented); the underwater Genie; the lamp's skill restrictions (members' skills on free worlds, Construction without a house, Runecraft/Herblore/Sailing before their quests), which belong to the shared lamp chooser. Other random events could build on the same schedule.

